A task's demos are evidence to reconcile, not examples to cherry-pick. Before inferring a rule, compare each pair's dimensions, palette, geometry, and exact input/output difference. If a new pair has different dimensions/palette or is an identity mapping while earlier pairs showed changes, do not force a single transformation from superficial commonalities. Consider conditional task variants or an unresolved inconsistency; request a further demo only if it can distinguish hypotheses. Validate every proposed rule against every pair before submission. An incorrect submission should trigger re-analysis of the rule and the full evidence set rather than another unvalidated guess.
